# Monitor profiles: one .conf file per layout you want to switch to, in this folder.

# Give each a unique name ending in .conf, e.g. Mirror.conf, Office.conf.
# (Suggest not to call one "default" - that name ships with the dotfiles.)

# tip: try the layout live with wdisplays (Quick Settings > «Мониторы
# (wdisplays)»), write it into ~/.config/mango/monitors.conf as monitor_rule
# lines (`wlr-randr` shows names, modes and positions), then copy that file
# here under its new name:
#     cp ~/.config/mango/monitors.conf ~/.config/mango/Monitor_Profiles/Office.conf
# SUPER SHIFT E > «Профиль мониторов» copies <name>.conf over
# ~/.config/mango/monitors.conf.

# Picking a profile overwrites ~/.config/mango/monitors.conf and keeps no
# backup of it - save the current layout as a profile first if you want it back.

# The profile loads on its own: mango reloads its config when a sourced file
# changes. `mmsg get all-monitors` lists names, sizes and positions.
